  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Suppose that \\(P = 2^m\\) and \\(Q = 3^n.\\) Which of the following is equal to \\(12^{mn}\\) for every pair of integers \\((m, n)?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(P^2 Q\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(P^n Q^m\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(P^n Q^{2m}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(P^{2m} Q^n\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(P^{2n} Q^m\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2009-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(12 = 2^2 \\cdot 3,\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} 12^{mn} &= 2^{2mn} \\cdot 3^{mn} \\\\ &= (2^m)^{2n}(3^n)^m \\\\ &= P^{2n}Q^m. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(12 = 2^2 \\cdot 3\\)",
        "Then \\(12^{mn} = 2^{2mn} \\cdot 3^{mn}\\) \\(= (2^m)^{2n}(3^n)^m\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
